  "worked_solution": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}+3(3)-18}{{3}^{2}-3(3)}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & =\\frac{(y+6)(y-3)}{y(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+6}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{2}+3y-18}{{y}^{2}-3y} & ={lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{y+6}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+6}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
